  <iati-identifier>GB-GOV-1-301035-407</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="GB-GOV-1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UK - Foreign, Commonwealth Development Office (FCDO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global Dashboard of Illicit Finance Vulnerabilities (ICE ODA Project)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project, led by Tax Justice Network with input from the University of Sussex, has three interlinked components. The first component will produce an update of bilateral and jurisdiction-level Illicit Financial Flows vulnerability assessments, based on secrecy and regulatory data and aggregate trade and investment flows. The second component will see the construction and analysis of granular datasets of investment stock values and network architectures in / by key countries and actors and concern. The final component will see the integration of FDI and sanctions datasets from component 2, with updated TJN IFF vulnerability assessment in component 1, to support fine-grained, targeted assessment of risks associated with IFFs from particular countries of interest. Illicit financial flows are when money or capital is illegally earned, utilised, or transferred between countries. Illicit financial flows can involve an array of actors at different levels &#x2013; across both developing and wealthier countries. Developing countries rich in natural resources, as well as those with high volumes of trade with advanced economies, show particularly high levels of illicit outflows. This project is seeking to map those illicit financial flows, across multiple ODA jurisdictions, and to estimate and measure the scale and risks of illicit financial flows using three main indicators of IFF risks: vulnerability, exposure, and intensity.</narrative>
  </description>
